== en
titulo: Food
intro: Learn basic food words and meal times, along with their key verbs.
b1.titulo: The three meals of the day
b1.texto: "The three main meals are **el desayuno** (breakfast), **la comida** or **el almuerzo** (lunch), and **la cena** (dinner).\nEach meal has an equivalent verb:\n- **desayunar** → *Desayuno café con pan.* (I have coffee and bread for breakfast)\n- **comer** → *Como arroz o verdura a las dos.* (I eat / have lunch at two)\n- **cenar** → *Ceno huevos con patatas.* (I have eggs and potatoes for dinner)\n\nPhysical needs use the verb **tener**:\n- **Tengo hambre** (I am hungry).\n- **Tengo sed** (I am thirsty).\n\nWith gustar, foods take definite articles: *Me gustan **las** manzanas*."
b2.titulo: What do you eat?
b3.titulo: Food vocabulary
b4.titulo: Meal verbs and physical sensations
b4.texto: Notice the use of meal verbs like cenar and idioms with tener like tener hambre.
b5.titulo: Daily meals
b6.titulo: Vocabulary check
b6.pregunta: Which meal is eaten in the morning?
b6.o0.refuerzo: Exactly! Breakfast is the morning meal.
b6.o1.refuerzo: La cena is dinner, eaten in the evening.
b6.o2.refuerzo: La comida is lunch, eaten at midday.
b7.titulo: Complete with the article
b7.pregunta: Choose the right article for general preferences.
b7.o0.refuerzo: Correct! Gustar takes the definite plural article las.
b7.o1.refuerzo: Manzanas is plural feminine, so it requires las.
b7.o2.refuerzo: General preferences use the definite article.
b8.titulo: Order the words
b8.traduccion: I don't like cold milk.
b9.titulo: Write the phrase
b9.pregunta: Translate into Spanish: «I'm hungry.»
